// `vue-tsc --build` keeps each project's `.tsbuildinfo` in the checkout's own
// `../.cache/tsbuildinfo`, beside the other tools' caches, never in
// `node_modules`: a worktree's `node_modules` may be a link to the main
// checkout's. `--build` reads an input again only when it is newer than the
// buildinfo, so a build in one checkout counted a type error written earlier in
// another as up to date, and `npm run typecheck` passed there with no output.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.tests.json" }
  ]
}
